{"name":"Scalloped Shell","hex":"#f3e9e0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"scalloped","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of scallop"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an edge or border marked with semicircles.","Cooked gratin; baked in a typical type of sauce, usually with cheese, as a casserole, e.g. scalloped potatoes; scalloped corn"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scalloped"},{"term":"shell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard external covering of an animal.\nThe calcareous or chitinous external covering of mollusks, crustaceans, and some other invertebrates.","The calcareous or chitinous external covering of mollusks, crustaceans, and some other invertebrates."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove the outer covering or shell of something.","To bombard, to fire projectiles at, especially with artillery."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shell"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scallop","blocks":[{"text":"Scallop is a common name that encompasses various species of marine bivalve molluscs in the taxonomic family Pectinidae, the scallops. However, this common name is also sometimes applied to species in other closely related families within the superfamily Pectinoidea, which also includes the thorny oysters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Argopecten_irradians.jpg/330px-Argopecten_irradians.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scallop"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Opened_scallop_shell.jpg/500px-Opened_scallop_shell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Opened_scallop_shell.jpg/500px-Opened_scallop_shell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A live opened scallop showing the internal anatomy: The pale orange circular part is the adductor muscle; the darker orange curved part is the \"coral\", a culinary term for the ovary or roe.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOpened_scallop_shell.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Fast_and_slow_adductor_muscles_of_the_Yesso_scallop%2C_Patinopecten_yessoensis.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Fast_and_slow_adductor_muscles_of_the_Yesso_scallop%2C_Patinopecten_yessoensis.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Adductor muscles of a scallop. a: photo in a live scallop. b: after removal of organs and tissues.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFast_and_slow_adductor_muscles_of_the_Yesso_scallop%2C_Patinopecten_yessoensis.webp"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Scallop_eyes2.jpg/500px-Scallop_eyes2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Scallop_eyes2.jpg/1280px-Scallop_eyes2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Scallop_eyes2.jpg/500px-Scallop_eyes2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScallop_eyes2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2f/Argopecten_irradians_eye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2f/Argopecten_irradians_eye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArgopecten_irradians_eye.jpg"},{"sr